---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version: preview
Date: 2026-11-10
  Features:
    - Added the `cqesto-cadical`, `qfun` and `qfun-cadical` QBF solvers as alternatives to `cqesto` for `--encoding=qbf`, selected with `--qbf-solver` (which now takes the solver name or path); the assignment is now read from the line starting with `v` instead of its position in the output, so that any of them can drive the exploration. (#216)
    - Added `make install <solver>`, which builds one QBF solver (`cqesto`, `cqesto-cadical`, `qfun`, `qfun-cadical`), and `make setup all` now builds all of them; cadical is built once at a pinned revision and shared, and a solver is rebuilt when its revision, its SAT solver or the link mode changes. (#216)
    - Added `make setup macos`, which builds the native dependency that has no package on macOS (OpenSTA 2.0.17) into `.deps/`, installing python@3.14, `yosys`, cmake, swig and tcl-tk@8 from Homebrew. (#85)
    - Added `make setup all`, which additionally builds the QBF solvers at pinned revisions (see #216), and documented both in the README. (#85)
    - Added specific archivation approaches (.tar.gz, .tar.xz). (#210)
    - Further modularised Configuration Exploration. (#213)
    - Added the slash of inputs pass (`--slash=slash_it`). (#222)
    - Added `run_stats.csv` columns `slash_error`, `slash_area`, `slash_power`, `slash_delay` and `slash_time`, and a `gen_slash` row with iteration 0. (#222)
  Minor Features:
    - Added a class for csv formatting. (#213)
    - Added more multipliers verilogs. (#213)
  Major Changes:
    - Completely revised the Timer module and how it works. (#213)
    - Completely revised the argument parsing for Specifications; now more centralised and automated. (#213)
  Minor Changes:
    - `yosys`, `sta` and `cqesto` are now looked up in `.deps/bin` and then on the PATH, from every call site, and a missing executable raises an actionable error instead of a `FileNotFoundError`. (#85)
    - `make setup macos` and `make setup all` now verify the toolchain and fail when `yosys` or `sta` is missing or does not run. (#85)
    - `make py_init` recreates `.venv` when it was created by a different major.minor python version. (#85)
    - Added `make rm_deps`, and `make clean-all` now also removes `.deps/`. (#85)
    - On macOS `make setup macos` and `make setup all` refuse a repository path containing a space, which the OpenSTA build rules cannot handle. (#85)
    - Standardised Live/Append Storage interface. (#213)
    - Further modularised Configuration Exploration. (#213)
    - Rewritten all circuits verilogs to simplify understanding and extension. (#213)
    - Reorganised solve/synth/verify pipeline. (#213)
    - Now the default archivation is .tar.xz instead of .zip. (#210)
    - Removed zip archivation approach. (#210)
    - Updated `networkx` to 3.7, `pygraphviz` to 2.0.4 and `bidict` to 0.24.1 (`colorama`, `tabulate` and `typing_extensions` were already current). (#238)
    - The python environment is now created with Python 3.15 instead of 3.14, and `make setup macos` installs `python@3.15`; the pipeline was re-run on 3.15.2 with identical results. (#238)
    - Replaced `--slash-to-kill` with `--slash` (`none`, `slash_to_kill`, `slash_it`). (#222)
    - `--error-for-slash` no longer defaults to 1 and is required when `--slash` is not `none`. (#222)
    - The iterative slash pass now runs before the exploration loop, so it no longer consumes the first error partition. (#222)
  Bugfixes:
    - `make setup all` (and `make install`) now link the QBF solvers statically on Linux: the ones built on minisat would otherwise need its shared library at run time, which does not travel with the executable copied out of the build tree. (#216)
    - The generated solver and labelling scripts now run with the interpreter executing `main.py`, instead of whatever `python3` resolves to on the PATH. (#85)
    - Patched a bug when min-labelling, where no error is found (also added warning). (#213)
    - Updated `z3-solver` from 4.16.0 to 5.4.1: z3 optimises bit-vector objectives through its MaxSAT engine (`maxres`), which returned a non-optimal optimum on some circuits, so many labels of the generated circuits were wrong (most of them 0); with the fixed solver they match the true stuck-at weights. (#238)
  Minor Optimizations:
    - Optimised memory footprint of LiveStorage. (#213)
    - Shared one extraction implementation between subgraph extraction modes 55 and 6, each solving over only the nodes that can belong to its subgraph, which shrinks the z3 encoding. (#230)
